# Served by Cloudflare's static-asset layer as real 301s. History: the July 28
# staging test found _redirects ignored (all four rules 404ed), and the rules
# moved into astro.config.mjs `redirects`. That was the wrong lesson from a
# transient result: Astro static `redirects` emit meta-refresh HTML pages that
# serve as 200s (soft redirects), while this file — retested July 30 — now
# yields true 301s (proven by /ai-governance/.../dcam-2/). So everything is
# consolidated here and astro.config.mjs no longer declares redirects.
#
# Sources of these rules:
#   1. The four original governance/glossary rules (below, unchanged).
#   2. The seven rules formerly in astro.config.mjs.
#   3. The full WordPress Redirection plugin export of July 30, 2026
#      (C:\SRJ Website Code Archive\redirects.json, 53 rules), reconciled:
#      disabled rules dropped (ids 26, 32, 35); duplicate sources collapsed to
#      the rule WordPress actually fires (lowest position; ids 9, 18, 41, 43,
#      44, 45, 46 dropped); absolute srjconsultingservices.com targets made
#      root-relative so they hold on staging and production alike; the
#      "Ignore Case" garbage in id 2's target stripped.
#
# Every source was verified 404 on staging before being claimed (no rule
# shadows a live page), and every target verified 200, with one exception:
# ids 1-2 targeted /ai-business-enablement-audit/, a WordPress top-level page
# that does not exist on this site, so both are flattened to the canonical
# service URL.
#
# Deliberately preserved production chains (do not "fix" these):
#   /ai-glossary/ -> /resources/ai-glossary/ -> /ai-resources/ai-glossary/
#   /services/ai-it-security-audit/ -> /books/.../ai-it-security-audit/
#     -> /services/risk-governance-security/ai-it-security-audit/
# Both reproduce WordPress's own hop count so crawlers see no change at
